$$
where $\lambda$ absorbs the transform normalization and source strength. This is the <Yukawa potential>: a nonzero vector-field mass screens the interaction beyond the range $m^{-1}$. As $m\to0$, it tends to the long-range Coulomb potential $\lambda/r$. The same <limit> removes the mass term that broke gauge invariance in part (b).

