The normalization $g_{\mu\nu}\dot x^\mu\dot x^\nu=-1$ then rearranges to
$$
\frac12\dot r^2-\frac{m}{r}+\frac{h^2}{2r^2}-\frac{mh^2}{r^3}
=\frac{E^2-1}{2},
$$
so the displayed radial energy is also constant. This is the <effective potential for timelike Schwarzschild geodesics>.

